Fix the refund job retry cron, which failed with a TypeError on every run as long as a refund job was left in the table (IPET-3586).
Cron\Refund loads every job through the repository, so the refund column is unserialized into a RefundContext instead of being passed to plugin-core as a raw JSON string, and skips jobs without an external ID, because resubmitting them would create a new refund.
RefundService::createRefund() sets the external ID when the refund context is built, as 2.x did, so it is stored in the job: the refund webhook finds and deletes the job, and a resubmitted job is recognised by wallee as the same refund.

